    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0454" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg196"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Van Dyke</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d267-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 4, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>192. Department informed apples and similar American fruits must be consigned to
                    Netherlands Oversea Trust whereas fruits like oranges and lemons need not be so
                    consigned. Verify and if this discrimination exists, protest through most
                    effective channel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d267-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d267-f1-content">
                <p>The same to the Ambassador in Great Britain, No. 2072, September 4.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
